# NanoClaw — line-ending policy
#
# Shell scripts MUST be LF. They are executed inside Linux containers
# (container/entrypoint.sh is COPY'd into the agent image) and sourced by bash
# on the host. On Windows, core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check them out as
# CRLF, which corrupts the shebang — the agent container then fails on start
# with: "[FATAL tini] exec /app/entrypoint.sh failed: No such file or directory".
# Forcing LF here keeps the checkout correct on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
